                <pb facs="0511" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94116/96: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-07T21:00:00+01:00">September 7, 1938—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 9—8:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. My 167, August 9, 7 p.m. Chinese permanent delegate has addressed a further
                    communication to Secretary General containing additional information concerning
                    alleged use of poison gas by Japanese troops in China. Communication states that
                    after the first use of gas at Matang gas has continued to be used on many
                    occasions up to and including present drive on Hankow. Note asks that
                    communication be circulated to members of Council, Assembly and Advisory
                    Committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
